Packaging changes for the firestorm-git AUR package, newest first.
Firestorm's own release notes: https://www.firestormviewer.org/category/news/

2026-10-28
  * Fixed the build without LTO, for example with `!lto` in makepkg.conf or
    with AUR helpers that don't use LTO such as Shelly. GCC 16 reports false
    -Warray-bounds and -Wformat-truncation warnings there, which Firestorm's
    -Werror turned into errors. They are now kept as warnings.

2026-10-27
  * Now builds again with current upstream master and GCC 16: updated the
    _FORTIFY_SOURCE patch, added patches for -Wsfinae-incomplete and the
    WebRTC multiple-definition link error.
  * secondlife:// and hop:// links now open in Firestorm (the desktop entry
    registers itself as the handler for both).
  * Local patch, not in upstream Firestorm: opening a secondlife:// link while
    Firestorm is not running now starts the viewer. Before, it quit
    immediately.
  * Arguments containing spaces are now passed to Firestorm correctly.
  * Dependencies rebuilt from what the packaged binaries actually use:
    - Removed unused or bundled: apr-util, dbus-glib, gtk2, lib32-libidn,
      lib32-libsndfile, libbsd, libidn, libjpeg-turbo, libpng, libxss,
      libxml2, openal, sdl, zlib.
    - vlc replaced by libvlc: upstream now builds its VLC media plugin
      against the system libvlc, so the full VLC player isn't needed.
    - Added missing: alsa-lib, at-spi2-core, cairo, dbus, expat, fontconfig,
      glib2, libcups, libx11, libxcb, libxcomposite, libxdamage, libxext,
      libxfixes, libxkbcommon, libxrandr, nspr, pango, systemd-libs,
      util-linux-libs.
    - Added libxcursor (the viewer's cursors on X11) and libdecor (window
      decorations on Wayland, e.g. GNOME). SDL3 loads both at runtime.
    - The 32-bit voice client (Vivox) is only used for voice on OpenSim grids,
      so its libraries are now optional. For OpenSim voice, install:
        lib32-glibc lib32-gcc-libs lib32-util-linux lib32-zlib
        lib32-libidn11 (AUR)
      Second Life voice is not affected.
    - New optional dependencies: gst-plugins-good (in-world media; without
      it media faces stay blank), PulseAudio, PipeWire or JACK audio,
      libnotify, gtk3 (file picker), xdg-utils.
      See "pacman -Qi firestorm-git".
  * Packaging release notes, shown by "pacman -Qc firestorm-git".
  * Added hicolor-icon-theme (owns the icon directory the package installs to).
  * License corrected to LGPL-2.1-only (SPDX), matching the viewer source.
  * Build dependencies: removed boost (the build uses its own copy), added
    libxinerama, libpulse, gstreamer, gst-plugins-base-libs, libpipewire and
    wayland (required by the current upstream build configuration).
  * After upgrading, "pacman -Qdt" may list packages that were only installed
    for this package and are no longer needed.
